<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh 30-day T-bill yield falls to 5.68pct. [corrected 13:30 gmt]</title>
<headline>Bangladesh 30-day T-bill yield falls to 5.68pct. [corrected 13:30 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects yield figures in headline and text)</p>
<p>Bank, the central bank, sold 30-day treasury bills worth 620 million taka with a corresponding yield at 5.68 percent against 6.03 percent previously at an auction on Monday, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>The weighted average price against the bills was 99.53 taka per 100 taka against previous 99.43.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
